Use the Drupal AnnotationRegistry

doctrine/annotations 2.x removed AnnotationRegistry::registerLoader() —
autoloading is the only mechanism, so registering the class_exists
loader is built-in behaviour. Drupal core kept a copy of the class with
the method intact and calls it the same way this extractor does. Switch
to that copy, like the module already does for SimpleAnnotationReader
and StaticReflectionParser.

diff --git a/src/Extractor/AnnotationExtractor.php b/src/Extractor/AnnotationExtractor.php
--- a/src/Extractor/AnnotationExtractor.php
+++ b/src/Extractor/AnnotationExtractor.php
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ use Drupal\potion\Utility;
 use Drupal\Component\Annotation\Doctrine\StaticReflectionParser;
 use Drupal\Component\Annotation\Reflection\MockFileFinder;
 use Symfony\Component\Finder\SplFileInfo;
-use Doctrine\Common\Annotations\AnnotationRegistry;
+use Drupal\Component\Annotation\Doctrine\AnnotationRegistry;
 
 /**
  * Extract Annotation Translations from PHP files.
